    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1232">

                <pb facs="1333" n="1323" xml:id="pg1323"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.0066A/7–744: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Naples</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Brandt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-07T16:00:00-04:00">July 7, 1944—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>826. For Kirk. Algiers 27 to you<anchor n="81" xml:id="d1232-f1"/> regarding
                    enemy diplomats accredited to Vatican but who are not yet inside Vatican
                    City.</p>
                <p>We agree that such diplomats should either enter Vatican City, if feasible, or
                    that they be removed from Rome as soon as practicable to a safe and suitable
                    place where they would be held, with due regard for their diplomatic status,
                    pending their repatriation under safe conduct.</p>
                <p>Please repeat foregoing urgently to Myron C. Taylor (giving him substance of
                    Algiers’ aforesaid telegram, if you have not already done so) and inform him
                    that we are anxious to receive his comments by telegraph together with any
                    recommendations which he may wish to submit.<anchor n="82" xml:id="d1232-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Repeated to Algiers for Murphy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1232-f1" n="81" xml:id="d1232-f1-content">
                <p>Same as telegram 2221 from Algiers, <ref target="#pg1321">p. 1321</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1232-f2" n="82" xml:id="d1232-f2-content">
                <p>The substance of this telegram was transmitted to Mr. Taylor at Rome in a letter
                    dated July 8. The Personal Representative of President Roosevelt to Pope Pius
                    XII arrived in Rome to take up his duties on June 20.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
